credentials.description:
Device: {device_id} at {host}

Enter the local key for this device. You can find it in the Tuya IoT developer portal, or with a tool such as tuya-cloudcutter.

Protocol version {version} is preselected, {version_source}. Correct it if you know better — the other versions are tried automatically if this one fails, and whichever works is the one that gets stored.

live_capture.description:
Capture is running ({elapsed}s) — {count} datapoint(s) seen: {summary}

Press the doorbell, walk in front of it, and work through the Tuya app. A datapoint marked ⟳ has reported more than one value and behaves like an event; those are the ones a doorbell button and a motion sensor hide behind.

Worth doing while you are here: toggle every switch and setting in the Tuya app off and on again — night vision, the chime, the indicator light, recording mode, all of them. A datapoint only shows up once the device has reported it, and a setting that nobody touches never does. Switching each one twice returns it to where it was and reveals it at the same time.

Event candidates so far: {events}

Submit to refresh this screen. Tick 'Done' when you have triggered everything you want to find.
